From b4a4090f87c15b1f033670c6aa81dd76d01a3c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ihar Hrachyshka <ihar.hrachyshka@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:30:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libutil: Skip root chmod on Darwin when deleting

App Management can deny changing the mode of a launched app bundle even
when deleting it is allowed. Root does not need owner permission bits to
traverse and remove directories on Darwin, so avoid this unnecessary
operation.

Linux root normally bypasses these mode checks too, including in a
standard multi-user Nix daemon. However, UID 0 alone does not imply
CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE on Linux. A root process with that capability dropped
may still need chmod, so keep the UID-based shortcut specific to Darwin.

Add deletion tests for restrictive modes and a Darwin sandbox regression
that denies mode changes while allowing deletion. Put the regression in
an explicit Root* suite, excluded by default, and require root when it
is selected. It fails without this change and passes with it.

Fixes #6765

Assisted-by: GPT-6-Astra medium

Backport of https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16626 to Nix 2.35.3.
Adapt the Meson context and add a test main that preserves the default
GoogleTest behavior while excluding Root* suites unless selected explicitly.
